# Baseline security headers for static hosts that read this file natively
# (Cloudflare Pages, Netlify) — frontend/apps/web/nginx.conf (the container
# path) doesn't currently set any of its own, so this isn't a port of
# existing headers, it's a new baseline applied consistently to both
# deployment paths. Deliberately NOT a Content-Security-Policy: this app
# loads ECharts canvas rendering, an OIDC redirect flow, and fetches from a
# configurable API origin (VITE_API_BASE) — a CSP tight enough to matter but
# untested against all of that risks breaking the app in ways that are hard
# to catch before a real deploy; add one deliberately, tested against a real
# build, rather than by default here.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=()
